1. Pick up the package from Shelf A.
2. Place the parcel on the packing table.
3. Open the storage cabinet.
4. Close the dispatch room door.
5. Move the empty crate beside the packing station.
6. Pick up the barcode scanner from the workstation.
7. Place the shipping label roll on the packing table.
8. Move the trolley to the loading area.
9. Pick up the package and place it on the conveyor belt.
10. Open the storage cabinet and retrieve the packing tape.
11. Pick up the shipping box and place it on the packing station.
12. Retrieve the barcode scanner and place it on the inspection desk.
13. Open the supply cabinet and collect the bubble wrap.
14. Pick up the parcel and place it inside the dispatch cage.
15. Collect the empty carton and place it in the recycling area.
16. Pick up the delivery manifest and place it on the supervisor's desk.
17. Go to Shelf B, collect the package, and place it on the packing table.
18. Navigate to the receiving area, retrieve the parcel, and deliver it to Shelf C.
19. Go to the packing station, collect the sealed box, and place it in the dispatch area.
20. Navigate to the storage room, retrieve the packing tape, and place it on the packing station.
21. Go to Shelf D, collect the fragile package, and place it in the inspection area.
22. Navigate to the loading dock, retrieve the empty crate, and return it to storage.
23. Go to the inspection station, collect the approved parcel, and deliver it to the dispatch area.
24. Navigate to the workstation, retrieve the barcode scanner, and return it to the charging station.
25. If the package is labeled as fragile, place it in the fragile goods section; otherwise move it to the standard dispatch area.
26. If Shelf A is full, place the incoming package on Shelf B.
27. If the packing station has no packing tape, retrieve a new roll from the supply cabinet.
28. If the dispatch trolley is available, load the package onto it; otherwise place the package in the dispatch queue.
29. If the barcode scanner is on the workstation, return it to the charging station; otherwise inspect the charging station.
30. If a package is waiting in the inspection area, deliver it to dispatch; otherwise organize the packing station.
31. If the storage cabinet is open, close it before leaving the storage room.
32. Carry the fragile package without tilting or dropping it.
33. Transport the stacked cartons without disturbing the stack.
34. Move the sealed parcel without damaging its shipping label.
35. Deliver the package to the dispatch area without colliding with warehouse equipment.
36. Carry the liquid container while keeping it upright.
37. Place the heavy box on the lower shelf without stacking it on fragile items.
38. Transport the barcode scanner carefully without placing it on the floor.
39. Collect all packages from the receiving area, place them on their designated shelves according to their labels, and return to the packing station.
40. Prepare outgoing shipments by collecting packages from Shelves A, B, and C, placing them on the packing table, sealing them, and delivering them to the dispatch area.
41. Inspect the warehouse for misplaced packages, empty cartons, and unused packing materials, return every item to its designated location, and finish at the supervisor's desk.
42. Restock the packing station by collecting tape, labels, bubble wrap, and empty boxes from storage, arranging them neatly, and returning to the workstation.
43. Collect all approved parcels from the inspection area, sort them into fragile and standard shipments, place them in their respective dispatch sections, and return to the loading dock.
44. Prepare the warehouse for the next shift by organizing shelves, clearing the packing station, parking the trolley in its designated location, returning the barcode scanner to its charger, and closing all storage cabinets.
45. Inspect every storage aisle for misplaced packages, open cabinets, abandoned equipment, and blocked pathways, correct each issue, and return to the warehouse entrance.